  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The texts of Shakespeare's 150 sonnets have been "stripped ... bare ... to make the space of the poems open, porous, possible ..."--Working note. The full text of Shakespeare is printed in light gray type, with the author's selected words printed in darker type. The title is derived in this manner from the word Sonnets.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"NETS was designed and typeset by Anna Moschovakis and Jen Bervin using Caslon for the text and Hoefler Text for the numbers. The covers were letterpressed by Breck Hostetter."</subfield>
  </datafield>
